# L §7.1: "A bare literal in a band row takes its unit as a bare `0` does in a def: ... the band's declared
# unit where it is the row's whole value (`kz: (13000, 85528] = 525.12` in a band of `PLN` is 525.12 zł; in
# `0.12 * x - 3600`, 3600 is in x's unit)".  kz(10 000.00 PLN) = 525.12 PLN; kz(20 000.00 PLN) =
# 0.12 × 20 000 − 3 600 = -1 200 PLN (a num PLN: a band of num PLN, L §3.2 money × num → num CUR).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2027-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input a: money PLN
input b: money PLN
band kz(x: money PLN): num PLN

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  a = 10000.00
  b = 20000.00
  kz: [0, 13000] = 525.12 "row 1"
  kz: (13000, inf) = 0.12 * x - 3600 "row 2"

ask q1: kz(a), kz(b) law 2026-12-31
=== expect
q1: (525.12 PLN, -1 200 PLN)
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2027-01-01
